WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.400 --> 00:00:19.744
Hello. My name is Mohammad Ali Jaffry. I am an architect. With ten years of architectural experience. Welcome, to this episode. What AI changed.

2
00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:35.496
Here is the whole film, before the proof.

3
00:00:36.536 --> 00:00:39.775
Artificial intelligence changed the call to a model.

4
00:00:40.815 --> 00:00:43.335
It did not draw the business boundary.

5
00:00:44.375 --> 00:00:46.987
It did not become the owner of the fact.

6
00:00:48.027 --> 00:00:51.138
And a person still accepts the change.

7
00:00:52.458 --> 00:00:53.910
Five questions.

8
00:00:54.950 --> 00:00:55.925
One answer.

9
00:00:56.965 --> 00:00:57.963
Design.

10
00:00:59.003 --> 00:01:00.397
Boundaries.

11
00:01:01.437 --> 00:01:02.342
The pipes.

12
00:01:03.382 --> 00:01:04.636
Operations.

13
00:01:05.676 --> 00:01:06.651
And the bill.

14
00:01:07.691 --> 00:01:11.604
Every question is graded against a case a company wrote down.

15
00:01:11.984 --> 00:01:15.757
If a sentence is wider than the work it describes, we keep the narrower one.

16
00:01:16.457 --> 00:01:19.464
Silence is not evidence that the decision moved.

17
00:01:20.784 --> 00:01:22.015
Walk the dates.

18
00:01:23.055 --> 00:01:25.110
July 2024.

19
00:01:26.150 --> 00:01:28.472
Uber puts one door in front of every model.

20
00:01:29.172 --> 00:01:30.321
November.

21
00:01:31.361 --> 00:01:34.658
Anthropic publishes a standard port for tools.

22
00:01:35.698 --> 00:01:38.311
February 2025.

23
00:01:39.351 --> 00:01:43.426
A proxy, in the Envoy family, does the same job in public.

24
00:01:43.806 --> 00:01:44.688
April.

25
00:01:45.728 --> 00:01:48.398
Google announces a pipe between agents.

26
00:01:49.438 --> 00:01:50.170
May.

27
00:01:51.210 --> 00:01:55.018
GitHub’s agent opens a pull request, and then it waits.

28
00:01:55.398 --> 00:01:56.361
July.

29
00:01:57.401 --> 00:02:00.873
In Malaysia, a workshop draws six services.

30
00:02:01.913 --> 00:02:02.981
August.

31
00:02:04.021 --> 00:02:08.851
Shopify keeps one agent, and has to teach the judge not to cheat.

32
00:02:09.891 --> 00:02:12.503
May 2026.

33
00:02:13.543 --> 00:02:17.351
Netflix measures a smart router, and takes it off the path.

34
00:02:17.731 --> 00:02:18.695
July.

35
00:02:19.735 --> 00:02:22.730
The models move into the platform Netflix already ran.

36
00:02:23.710 --> 00:02:26.380
Start with the inside of a service.

37
00:02:27.420 --> 00:02:32.041
QRRA had a Java monolith, and an Oracle database, and a sale day that hurt.

38
00:02:32.421 --> 00:02:34.697
Eight thousand items.

39
00:02:35.737 --> 00:02:37.966
Two thousand orders in an hour.

40
00:02:39.006 --> 00:02:44.091
They slowed the door to fifty orders a batch, and bought stability by giving up speed.

41
00:02:44.471 --> 00:02:46.224
Then people sat down.

42
00:02:47.264 --> 00:02:48.135
Product.

43
00:02:49.175 --> 00:02:50.185
Engineering.

44
00:02:51.225 --> 00:02:52.444
Architects.

45
00:02:53.484 --> 00:02:55.527
They ran Event Storming.

46
00:02:56.567 --> 00:02:57.647
Events.

47
00:02:58.687 --> 00:02:59.743
Commands.

48
00:03:00.783 --> 00:03:02.780
Aggregates.

49
00:03:03.820 --> 00:03:05.771
Six bounded contexts.

50
00:03:06.811 --> 00:03:09.806
That is a human design, and it is a good one.

51
00:03:10.846 --> 00:03:14.213
It follows the business, and it follows a measured peak.

52
00:03:15.193 --> 00:03:16.319
Now the tool.

53
00:03:17.359 --> 00:03:22.561
Amazon Q Developer, in the section that describes the tool, writes the deployment code.

54
00:03:22.941 --> 00:03:26.226
Console clicks become infrastructure as code.

55
00:03:27.266 --> 00:03:28.462
Three days.

56
00:03:29.502 --> 00:03:31.127
That is construction.

57
00:03:32.167 --> 00:03:33.433
That is packaging.

58
00:03:34.473 --> 00:03:40.487
The last paragraph of the same post says the tool turned the monolith into six services in those three days.

59
00:03:40.867 --> 00:03:43.514
The workshop section does not say that.

60
00:03:44.554 --> 00:03:46.922
The research keeps them apart.

61
00:03:47.962 --> 00:03:51.016
A generated manifest is not the architecture.

62
00:03:52.336 --> 00:03:56.005
GitHub, the nineteenth of May, 2025.

63
00:03:57.045 --> 00:03:59.425
You assign an issue to Copilot.

64
00:04:00.465 --> 00:04:02.473
It reads the repository.

65
00:04:03.513 --> 00:04:06.125
It opens a draft pull request.

66
00:04:07.165 --> 00:04:09.638
And then the rules close around it.

67
00:04:10.678 --> 00:04:13.767
It may push only to a branch it created.

68
00:04:14.807 --> 00:04:17.094
You cannot approve your own request.

69
00:04:18.134 --> 00:04:21.477
The build does not run until a person says so.

70
00:04:22.517 --> 00:04:25.037
The pipeline is still a human checkpoint.

71
00:04:26.077 --> 00:04:28.178
The agent can prepare a change.

72
00:04:29.218 --> 00:04:30.994
It cannot accept it.

73
00:04:32.314 --> 00:04:34.915
Shopify’s Sidekick lives in the admin.

74
00:04:35.955 --> 00:04:37.058
One loop.

75
00:04:38.098 --> 00:04:39.665
A person speaks.

76
00:04:40.705 --> 00:04:42.366
The model chooses a tool.

77
00:04:43.406 --> 00:04:44.729
The tool runs.

78
00:04:45.769 --> 00:04:47.278
The result comes back.

79
00:04:48.318 --> 00:04:49.712
They published the scale.

80
00:04:50.752 --> 00:04:53.828
Under twenty tools, the behavior is clear.

81
00:04:54.868 --> 00:04:58.572
Between twenty and fifty, the boundaries blur.

82
00:04:59.612 --> 00:05:04.012
Past fifty, the prompt becomes what they call death by a thousand instructions.

83
00:05:04.392 --> 00:05:05.994
And here is the decision.

84
00:05:07.034 --> 00:05:09.124
They did not split the agent.

85
00:05:10.164 --> 00:05:13.380
They said a single agent can hold more than a team expects.

86
00:05:13.760 --> 00:05:16.616
The fashionable cut was the one they refused.

87
00:05:17.936 --> 00:05:19.387
Then the model cheated.

88
00:05:20.427 --> 00:05:25.780
Asked for customers whose status is enabled, it filtered on a tag that merely contained the word.

89
00:05:26.160 --> 00:05:28.876
The store already had a field for that.

90
00:05:29.916 --> 00:05:33.004
The store’s language was the authority.

91
00:05:34.044 --> 00:05:37.713
Shopify did not cut a new service to hold the wrong fact.

92
00:05:38.753 --> 00:05:41.249
They taught the judge the cheat.

93
00:05:42.289 --> 00:05:46.051
Syntax checks rose from about ninety-three percent to about ninety-nine.

94
00:05:46.431 --> 00:05:49.008
The judge moved closer to the people.

95
00:05:50.048 --> 00:05:51.790
The shop did not move at all.

96
00:05:53.110 --> 00:05:55.316
Boundaries, and data.

97
00:05:56.356 --> 00:06:00.350
Netflix’s platform does not keep the business database.

98
00:06:01.390 --> 00:06:05.105
At request time it calls the services that own the facts.

99
00:06:05.805 --> 00:06:08.208
For training, it keeps snapshots.

100
00:06:09.248 --> 00:06:12.789
A snapshot that someone else writes would be a shared database.

101
00:06:13.169 --> 00:06:16.606
The post describes calls, and copies for reading.

102
00:06:17.646 --> 00:06:19.480
Not a second writer.

103
00:06:20.520 --> 00:06:22.354
GenRec goes further.

104
00:06:23.394 --> 00:06:28.364
An unconstrained model invents titles that are not in the catalog.

105
00:06:29.404 --> 00:06:33.583
So the ranker scores only titles that exist.

106
00:06:34.623 --> 00:06:38.071
The legal set of identities stays a set the business owns.

107
00:06:39.051 --> 00:06:40.282
Now the pipes.

108
00:06:41.322 --> 00:06:43.191
This is the center of the film.

109
00:06:44.231 --> 00:06:49.305
Netflix built Switchboard, and every client had to pass through it.

110
00:06:50.005 --> 00:06:51.003
It routed.

111
00:06:52.043 --> 00:06:53.680
It enriched.

112
00:06:54.720 --> 00:06:57.971
It split traffic for experiments.

113
00:06:59.011 --> 00:07:05.211
It also sat on the path of more than thirty services, in front of a platform doing a million requests a second.

114
00:07:05.591 --> 00:07:07.355
The cost, written down.

115
00:07:08.395 --> 00:07:10.369
Ten to twenty milliseconds.

116
00:07:11.409 --> 00:07:13.023
Some clients timed out.

117
00:07:14.063 --> 00:07:18.475
A noisy neighbor, or one defect, and every experience behind it degraded.

118
00:07:18.855 --> 00:07:20.550
That is the old warning.

119
00:07:21.590 --> 00:07:24.132
A pipe that knows too much fails for everyone.

120
00:07:25.112 --> 00:07:27.539
They did not throw the policy away.

121
00:07:28.579 --> 00:07:30.402
They took it off the bytes.

122
00:07:31.442 --> 00:07:33.624
Lightbulb answers a small question.

123
00:07:34.664 --> 00:07:35.744
Which model.

124
00:07:36.784 --> 00:07:38.456
Which experiment.

125
00:07:39.496 --> 00:07:44.279
Envoy, already sitting on the way out of every application, carries the payload.

126
00:07:44.979 --> 00:07:48.938
The body is not opened in the middle, just to choose a door.

127
00:07:49.978 --> 00:07:52.730
The pipe that carries the payload is Envoy.

128
00:07:53.770 --> 00:07:55.360
Smart endpoints.

129
00:07:56.400 --> 00:07:57.538
A dumb pipe.

130
00:07:58.578 --> 00:08:03.118
Said again, in 2026, because a model router had forgotten it.

131
00:08:04.098 --> 00:08:08.057
Uber’s door is older, and it is honest about its thickness.

132
00:08:08.437 --> 00:08:10.573
One Go service.

133
00:08:11.613 --> 00:08:14.062
Callers speak the OpenAI shape.

134
00:08:15.102 --> 00:08:17.355
The gateway speaks to the vendors.

135
00:08:18.395 --> 00:08:23.852
Before a third party sees a request, personal data is replaced, and restored on the way home.

136
00:08:24.232 --> 00:08:25.985
That is logic in the pipe.

137
00:08:27.025 --> 00:08:28.778
It is not a saga.

138
00:08:29.818 --> 00:08:33.440
It does not decide that a trip is finished.

139
00:08:34.480 --> 00:08:36.454
About thirty teams.

140
00:08:37.494 --> 00:08:40.849
Sixteen million queries a month.

141
00:08:41.889 --> 00:08:45.825
The redactor costs latency, and it costs the quality of the answer.

142
00:08:46.205 --> 00:08:47.702
They published the tax.

143
00:08:48.742 --> 00:08:54.791
In February 2025, Bloomberg and Tetrate shipped the same idea as a proxy.

144
00:08:55.171 --> 00:08:56.553
One API.

145
00:08:57.593 --> 00:08:59.102
Many providers.

146
00:09:00.142 --> 00:09:03.358
And in April, Google announced a pipe between agents.

147
00:09:03.738 --> 00:09:07.569
PayPal, Salesforce, and ServiceNow were in the room.

148
00:09:08.609 --> 00:09:12.325
No compensation was published.

149
00:09:13.365 --> 00:09:18.009
A new pipe can exist, and still not be the broker of these estates.

150
00:09:19.329 --> 00:09:20.594
Operations.

151
00:09:21.634 --> 00:09:23.294
Keep the loops apart.

152
00:09:24.334 --> 00:09:27.028
The platform loop reconciles a deployment.

153
00:09:28.068 --> 00:09:28.881
Health.

154
00:09:29.921 --> 00:09:31.174
Scale.

155
00:09:32.214 --> 00:09:33.120
Rollback.

156
00:09:34.160 --> 00:09:35.646
The pin of the engine.

157
00:09:36.686 --> 00:09:41.156
The domain loop enforces the business rule, in the service that owns the fact.

158
00:09:41.536 --> 00:09:44.682
The decode loop only chooses the next token.

159
00:09:45.722 --> 00:09:51.144
Netflix put a mask in that third loop, so an illegal token is never chosen.

160
00:09:52.184 --> 00:09:53.101
Useful.

161
00:09:54.141 --> 00:09:54.954
Narrow.

162
00:09:55.994 --> 00:09:59.349
It cannot decide that a picked-up delivery stays active.

163
00:10:00.329 --> 00:10:03.000
Here is a failure the old tests miss.

164
00:10:04.040 --> 00:10:06.257
A caller asked for JSON.

165
00:10:07.297 --> 00:10:12.510
The front door accepted the request, dropped the constraint, and returned ordinary text.

166
00:10:13.210 --> 00:10:14.324
No error.

167
00:10:15.364 --> 00:10:18.313
A retry would have retried the wrong success.

168
00:10:19.353 --> 00:10:20.538
They patched it.

169
00:10:21.578 --> 00:10:23.017
The lesson is sharp.

170
00:10:24.057 --> 00:10:27.401
A timeout does not notice a well formed wrongness.

171
00:10:28.441 --> 00:10:31.552
The contract has to be checked.

172
00:10:32.592 --> 00:10:35.704
Design for failure moved onto the model call.

173
00:10:36.744 --> 00:10:39.147
The patterns did not become optional.

174
00:10:40.187 --> 00:10:42.416
They live in the platform, and in the proxy.

175
00:10:43.116 --> 00:10:45.253
Not as a new excuse to skip them.

176
00:10:46.573 --> 00:10:48.314
The new price is the token.

177
00:10:49.354 --> 00:10:52.338
GenRec says serving cost tracks the length of the prompt.

178
00:10:52.718 --> 00:10:56.607
Cut the tokens to about a third, and the bill falls by about as much.

179
00:10:57.307 --> 00:11:00.024
The ranking metric they plot barely moves.

180
00:11:01.064 --> 00:11:04.280
The context window is the new feature budget.

181
00:11:05.320 --> 00:11:10.869
What used to be a decision about which features to compute is now a decision about which history to keep.

182
00:11:11.569 --> 00:11:14.170
And the old price came back with numbers.

183
00:11:15.210 --> 00:11:17.555
Those ten to twenty milliseconds.

184
00:11:18.595 --> 00:11:22.322
That single point of failure.

185
00:11:23.362 --> 00:11:27.112
Shopify’s refusal to split one agent into many.

186
00:11:28.152 --> 00:11:31.856
Distribution, measured, and then partly unwound.

187
00:11:32.896 --> 00:11:34.927
You have seen this shape before.

188
00:11:36.247 --> 00:11:38.117
Nine characteristics.

189
00:11:39.157 --> 00:11:42.582
From the article of March 2014.

190
00:11:43.622 --> 00:11:46.919
Hold them up to these cases, and only these cases.

191
00:11:47.959 --> 00:11:54.054
The business services are still components, still cut around the work, still owned by people who accept the change.

192
00:11:54.434 --> 00:11:57.708
The pipe was stressed, and in the measured case it was restored.

193
00:11:58.088 --> 00:12:00.561
Governance of the model moved to the center.

194
00:12:01.601 --> 00:12:04.341
One door.

195
00:12:05.381 --> 00:12:06.310
One engine.

196
00:12:07.350 --> 00:12:10.775
A version pin an author may not override.

197
00:12:11.815 --> 00:12:15.123
The data did not become a shared writable store.

198
00:12:16.163 --> 00:12:19.298
Automation moved, in the development tools.

199
00:12:20.338 --> 00:12:22.718
Failure design moved onto the call.

200
00:12:23.758 --> 00:12:25.384
Evolution held.

201
00:12:26.424 --> 00:12:27.991
Measure the cost.

202
00:12:29.031 --> 00:12:30.970
Then pull the hot path back.

203
00:12:32.290 --> 00:12:35.831
So the article can say it at this grain, and no wider.

204
00:12:36.211 --> 00:12:39.346
People still draw the bounded contexts.

205
00:12:40.386 --> 00:12:42.406
People still own the facts.

206
00:12:43.446 --> 00:12:45.524
People still accept the change.

207
00:12:46.564 --> 00:12:49.861
What acquired an architecture of its own is the call to the model.

208
00:12:50.241 --> 00:12:53.585
And the cost of that call now sits inside the microservice premium.

209
00:12:54.565 --> 00:12:56.840
Three things to carry away.

210
00:12:57.880 --> 00:12:58.484
One.

211
00:12:59.524 --> 00:13:03.413
The call to the model acquired a door, a runtime, a proxy, and a bill.

212
00:13:04.113 --> 00:13:04.647
Two.

213
00:13:05.687 --> 00:13:11.458
The boundary, the owner of the fact, and the person who accepts a change did not move.

214
00:13:12.498 --> 00:13:13.229
Three.

215
00:13:14.269 --> 00:13:18.634
Where a closing sentence is wider than the work, keep the narrower one.

216
00:13:19.614 --> 00:13:22.169
That is the end of what was written down.

217
00:13:23.209 --> 00:13:26.018
The article itself is still to be written from this evidence.

218
00:13:26.398 --> 00:13:28.743
Thank you for staying to the last line.
